  "description": "Stramash – Fast and forgiving gravel. Built for the long way round.\n\nStramash means ‘a racket’ or ‘disturbance’ to the Scots, the perfect name for this unruly take on big-tyre, drop bar adventure. Blurring MTB and gravel, it’s handmade around a beautiful and versatile Columbus Life steel frame, with updated geometry and room for up to 50mm rubber.\n\nCrafted as the antidote to the fatigue and compromise often found in ultra-endurance setups, the Stramash offers the performance and comfort to keep you pushing further, without punishing your hands, back, or backside. We’ve carefully refined the geometry, increased tyre clearance, and built in all the versatility you need to take on truly challenging terrain.\n\nPacked with features for modern adventure riding, whether you’re grinding gravel, tackling trails or venturing into the unknown, the Shand Stramash is built to take you there, and beyond.\n\nMade for riders who want to cover big distances fast on gravel, and for loaded bikepacking trips. If your riding is mostly road or heavy touring, look at the Stooshie or the Stoater.",
